00:10:10.793 --> 00:10:11.894
Now it’s day three—

00:10:11.894 --> 00:10:12.745
Shoulder day.

00:10:12.745 --> 00:10:14.246
Shoulders are widely considered

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:15.931
the highest bang-for-buck muscle group.

00:10:15.931 --> 00:10:17.967
If you’ve got thick, broad shoulders,

00:10:17.967 --> 00:10:20.169
your overall proportions will look super balanced.

00:10:20.269 --> 00:10:21.587
Visually, it also makes

00:10:21.587 --> 00:10:22.705
your waist look smaller,

00:10:22.705 --> 00:10:23.823
and your head look smaller.

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:24.740
First movement—

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:25.841
Seated shoulder press.

00:10:25.841 --> 00:10:28.644
You can use any shoulder press machine at the gym,

00:10:28.644 --> 00:10:29.929
or use the Smith machine.

00:10:29.929 --> 00:10:31.831
Personally, I prefer the Smith machine—

00:10:31.831 --> 00:10:34.183
but it does require a few extra setup steps.

00:10:34.183 --> 00:10:36.152
So today I’ll demo with the shoulder press machine.

00:10:36.152 --> 00:10:37.803
Super simple, same great effect.

00:10:37.803 --> 00:10:40.389
Just adjust the seat height properly.

00:10:40.389 --> 00:10:41.774
At the bottom of the movement,

00:10:41.774 --> 00:10:43.526
your elbows should be slightly below shoulder level.

00:10:43.526 --> 00:10:46.028
If the handles are too low, the pressing angle becomes awkward—

00:10:46.028 --> 00:10:47.463
and increases shoulder joint pressure.

00:10:47.463 --> 00:10:50.032
Inhale, brace your core, and press upward.

00:10:50.032 --> 00:10:52.652
Exhale slowly during the movement.

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:54.837
Try to keep your back pressed against the seat.

00:10:55.087 --> 00:10:58.407
This movement mainly targets the anterior delts,

00:10:58.574 --> 00:11:01.844
but also works the lateral delts and triceps.

00:11:02.178 --> 00:11:04.013
If your elbows flare out too much,

00:11:04.013 --> 00:11:05.765
it may increase shoulder impingement.

00:11:05.765 --> 00:11:06.615
So during training,

00:11:06.615 --> 00:11:09.368
try moving your elbows slightly forward.

00:11:09.368 --> 00:11:10.619
At the top of the press,

00:11:10.619 --> 00:11:12.621
don’t fully lock out your elbows,

00:11:12.888 --> 00:11:15.091
and don’t completely release the weight.

00:11:15.257 --> 00:11:18.344
Keep tension on the shoulders throughout the movement.

00:11:18.828 --> 00:11:21.197
Slow press, slow release.

00:11:21.197 --> 00:11:22.415
For this movement, I use

00:11:22.415 --> 00:11:24.667
50 kg per side, 12 reps, 3 sets.

00:11:24.667 --> 00:11:26.068
Rest 90 seconds between sets.

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:27.787
Second movement—

00:11:27.787 --> 00:11:29.038
Machine lateral raise.

00:11:29.038 --> 00:11:30.990
We’re using the most common,

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:32.992
standard lateral raise machine.

00:11:32.992 --> 00:11:35.578
It’s great for isolating the lateral delts,

00:11:35.578 --> 00:11:37.012
sculpting shoulder width,

00:11:37.012 --> 00:11:38.714
and building that V-taper look(wide shoulders, narrow waist).

00:11:38.714 --> 00:11:40.032
Adjust the seat height

00:11:40.032 --> 00:11:41.634
so the pads sit roughly

00:11:41.634 --> 00:11:43.669
on your upper arm near the elbow.

00:11:43.669 --> 00:11:44.437
While performing,

00:11:44.437 --> 00:11:47.390
watch out for overcompensation from your traps.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.442
You can lean forward slightly—

00:11:49.642 --> 00:11:52.011
then raise your elbows forward and outward.

00:11:52.011 --> 00:11:54.914
Remember: it’s an outward and upward arc,

00:11:54.914 --> 00:11:56.348
not a straight lift.

00:11:56.599 --> 00:11:58.033
The easiest way to check—

00:11:58.033 --> 00:12:00.519
see if you’re shrugging during the movement.

00:12:00.669 --> 00:12:03.139
Compare both forms side by side.

00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:04.890
For pacing, I go with:

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.560
slow lift, pause, slow release.

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.378
Avoid explosive thrusts—

00:12:09.478 --> 00:12:11.497
stay controlled and steady.

00:12:11.497 --> 00:12:14.016
Feel the weight sitting firmly on your shoulders.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.084
For this movement, I use

00:12:15.084 --> 00:12:17.019
32 kg, 12 reps, 3 sets.

00:12:17.019 --> 00:12:18.521
Rest 90 seconds between sets.

00:12:18.704 --> 00:12:19.505
Final movement—

00:12:19.505 --> 00:12:20.506
Cable pushdown.

00:12:20.506 --> 00:12:22.308
Targeting the triceps.

00:12:22.308 --> 00:12:24.744
Find a cable machine and a V-rope attachment.

00:12:24.744 --> 00:12:27.296
Adjust the height to about shoulder level.

00:12:27.296 --> 00:12:29.498
Use your body to help bring the rope down into position.

00:12:29.498 --> 00:12:32.151
You can stand staggered or feet parallel—

00:12:32.151 --> 00:12:35.020
just make sure your body stays stable and doesn’t swing.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.423
Your elbows should be the only pivot point.

00:12:38.073 --> 00:12:40.426
Keep your upper arms close to your body, elbows fixed.

00:12:40.426 --> 00:12:42.945
Try to keep the rope parallel to the machine’s cable

00:12:42.945 --> 00:12:44.864
so the force line stays consistent.

00:12:44.864 --> 00:12:47.082
That way, you can check if your form is consistent.

00:12:47.082 --> 00:12:50.419
Training rhythm: slow press, pause, slow release.

00:12:50.669 --> 00:12:51.604
For this movement, I use

00:12:51.604 --> 00:12:53.439
20 kg, 12 reps, 3 sets.

00:12:53.439 --> 00:12:55.007
Rest 90 seconds between sets.

00:12:56.025 --> 00:12:57.676
Now we’re on day four—

00:12:57.676 --> 00:12:58.394
Back day.

00:12:58.394 --> 00:12:59.795
Training your back has tons of benefits.

00:12:59.795 --> 00:13:01.497
It improves posture,

00:13:01.497 --> 00:13:02.698
and also helps with

00:13:02.698 --> 00:13:04.583
daily function and athletic performance.

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:05.618
Today we’ll do

00:13:05.618 --> 00:13:07.136
two vertical pulls and one horizontal pull—

00:13:07.136 --> 00:13:08.904
all using the cable machine.

00:13:08.904 --> 00:13:09.772
Super simple.

00:13:10.089 --> 00:13:10.956
First movement—

00:13:10.956 --> 00:13:12.374
Overhand lat pulldown.

00:13:12.374 --> 00:13:14.643
A classic back training exercise.

00:13:14.643 --> 00:13:15.711
Grip wider than shoulder width—

00:13:15.711 --> 00:13:17.830
about 1.5 times your shoulder width.

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:18.814
Palms facing forward.

00:13:18.814 --> 00:13:20.866
Use your body to help bring the bar down into position,

00:13:20.866 --> 00:13:23.369
and lock your legs under the thigh pads.

00:13:23.369 --> 00:13:24.069
During training,

00:13:24.069 --> 00:13:26.739
scapular and torso stability are key.

00:13:26.789 --> 00:13:29.141
As you pull down, let your scapula naturally depress.

00:13:29.175 --> 00:13:31.994
Pull the bar down to your upper chest or collarbone.

00:13:32.294 --> 00:13:33.813
Squeeze your scapula inward,

00:13:33.813 --> 00:13:35.314
and feel your back muscles contract.

00:13:35.314 --> 00:13:37.483
Lean back slightly, then return upright.

00:13:37.566 --> 00:13:39.685
No need to over-control your torso angle.

00:13:39.685 --> 00:13:42.238
You can practice scapular control with just bodyweight.

00:13:42.471 --> 00:13:43.956
Raise both arms overhead.

00:13:43.956 --> 00:13:45.357
Relax your scapula.

00:13:45.357 --> 00:13:47.109
Then depress your scapula.

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.929
Relax, then squeeze downward.

00:13:50.212 --> 00:13:52.147
That’s exactly what you want during training.

00:13:53.082 --> 00:13:56.886
Training tempo: slow pull, pause, slow release.

00:13:56.886 --> 00:13:58.604
Control the movement—don’t bounce.

00:13:58.604 --> 00:14:00.806
Compare both forms side by side.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:02.424
Keep control when releasing the bar.

00:14:02.424 --> 00:14:04.410
No need to fully extend your arms—

00:14:04.493 --> 00:14:05.961
keep tension on your back.

00:14:05.961 --> 00:14:07.363
If your body swings too much,

00:14:07.363 --> 00:14:08.831
using momentum to pull—

00:14:08.914 --> 00:14:09.999
you might lift heavier,

00:14:09.999 --> 00:14:12.918
but it won’t be as effective as slow, controlled reps.

00:14:12.918 --> 00:14:13.769
For this movement, I use

00:14:13.769 --> 00:14:15.838
63 kg, 12 reps, 3 sets.

00:14:15.838 --> 00:14:17.306
Rest 90 seconds between sets.

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.275
Second movement—

00:14:19.275 --> 00:14:20.726
Underhand lat pulldown.

00:14:20.726 --> 00:14:22.228
You can use the same cable machine,

00:14:22.228 --> 00:14:26.065
or an underhand lat pulldown station for more lat focus.

00:14:26.065 --> 00:14:27.883
Grip slightly narrower than shoulder width.

00:14:27.883 --> 00:14:29.602
Keep your chest up and scapula engaged.

00:14:29.718 --> 00:14:31.120
Lift your chest slightly.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.721
Maintain a natural curve in your back.

00:14:32.905 --> 00:14:35.307
As you pull down, let your scapula naturally depress.

00:14:35.524 --> 00:14:36.725
Then activate your back muscles.

00:14:36.809 --> 00:14:39.445
Avoid shrugging or pulling with your arms.

00:14:39.445 --> 00:14:42.965
Training tempo: slow pull, pause, slow release.

00:14:43.048 --> 00:14:45.885
Avoid bouncing or using momentum to lift.

00:14:46.085 --> 00:14:46.952
For this movement, I use

00:14:46.952 --> 00:14:48.888
56 kg, 12 reps, 3 sets.

00:14:48.888 --> 00:14:50.456
Rest 90 seconds between sets.

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:51.840
Final movement—

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:53.058
Seated row.

00:14:53.058 --> 00:14:54.510
Because of the movement path,

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:56.145
both vertical and horizontal pulls

00:14:56.145 --> 00:14:58.197
train the back muscles—

00:14:58.197 --> 00:15:00.816
but horizontal pulls help build thickness.

00:15:00.816 --> 00:15:03.602
They activate more rhomboids and traps.

00:15:03.602 --> 00:15:06.138
You can use a cable or rowing machine.

00:15:06.488 --> 00:15:08.757
Feet on the pedals, knees slightly bent.

00:15:08.757 --> 00:15:10.826
Keep your lower back straight and chest up.

00:15:10.826 --> 00:15:12.161
Let your back stay natural.

00:15:12.161 --> 00:15:13.913
Avoid hunching or shrugging.

00:15:13.913 --> 00:15:16.031
One special thing about this movement—

00:15:16.031 --> 00:15:19.435
narrow grip and wide grip target different muscles.

00:15:19.435 --> 00:15:22.705
I recommend starting with lighter weight and wide grip rows—

00:15:22.705 --> 00:15:23.505
to stimulate and strengthen

00:15:23.505 --> 00:15:26.025
your upper back, traps, and rhomboids.

00:15:26.025 --> 00:15:29.478
Training tempo: slow pull, pause, slow release.

00:15:29.645 --> 00:15:31.497
Don’t fully relax on the release—

00:15:31.497 --> 00:15:34.116
avoid leaning forward and using momentum to restart.

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.267
For this movement, I use

00:15:35.267 --> 00:15:37.419
49 kg, 12 reps, 3 sets.

00:15:37.419 --> 00:15:38.887
Rest 90 seconds between sets.

00:15:39.772 --> 00:15:41.523
That wraps up the full routine—

00:15:41.523 --> 00:15:43.926
a beginner-friendly, machine-based workout plan.

00:15:43.926 --> 00:15:46.295
4 days, 13 exercises, full-body training.

00:15:46.295 --> 00:15:47.813
This machine-based program

00:15:47.813 --> 00:15:49.048
is just a general framework.

00:15:49.048 --> 00:15:49.515
Meaning—

00:15:49.515 --> 00:15:51.834
if you focus on mastering these 13 movements,

00:15:51.834 --> 00:15:54.153
you’ll see noticeable improvements in your physique

00:15:54.153 --> 00:15:55.437
You may have noticed—

00:15:55.437 --> 00:15:57.006
every movement is 12 reps, 3 sets,

00:15:57.006 --> 00:15:58.173
with 90 seconds rest.

00:15:58.173 --> 00:15:58.907
Training tempo—

00:15:58.907 --> 00:16:01.310
slow, pause, slow release.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.244
This isn’t a strict rule—

00:16:02.244 --> 00:16:02.745
it’s just

00:16:02.745 --> 00:16:03.679
a general guideline.

00:16:03.679 --> 00:16:05.331
Once you’ve made progress,

00:16:05.331 --> 00:16:07.032
and built solid movement patterns,

00:16:07.032 --> 00:16:08.283
you can gradually add in

00:16:08.283 --> 00:16:09.685
heavy low-rep sets,

00:16:09.685 --> 00:16:11.870
or high-rep endurance sets.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:12.755
In short, my goal is—

00:16:12.755 --> 00:16:14.573
to help beginners who want to start training at the gym

00:16:14.573 --> 00:16:17.376
do it in the simplest and safest way possible.

00:16:17.376 --> 00:16:18.661
No need to memorize too much.

00:16:18.661 --> 00:16:20.512
Just spend an hour each time,

00:16:20.512 --> 00:16:22.331
and focus on doing 3–4 movements well.

00:16:22.331 --> 00:16:23.449
Once you’re familiar with everything,

00:16:23.449 --> 00:16:24.817
you can gradually add in

00:16:24.817 --> 00:16:26.502
free weight exercises.

00:16:26.502 --> 00:16:27.252
In the next video,

00:16:27.252 --> 00:16:29.822
I’ll release a full-body free weight workout.

00:16:29.822 --> 00:16:31.540
To help you train more completely.

